FFmpeg libswscale (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  The YUV to RGB stage in web/src/browser/yuv.ts (re-exported by web/src/browser/resample.ts) imitates the arithmetic of libswscale as PyAV runs it. It is written from that
  arithmetic, not from the FFmpeg source, but its filter construction (makeFilter) follows the expressions and tap count of swscale's
  initFilter, so it is treated as derived from an LGPL-2.1-or-later work. Those two files are therefore licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later (SPDX-License-Identifier
  in each header), not Apache-2.0; the full text is in LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt and also ships with the page (web/src/notices.txt, then
  src/inframe/web/dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt). The derived code stays in those two files, which are published as source here and whose complete source also
  ships with the built page and the wheel (src/inframe/web/dist/yuv.ts and src/inframe/web/dist/resample.ts, LGPL-2.1 section 4), so a user can read, modify and replace it
  and rebuild the page (npm --prefix web run build). The built page bundles them into minified JavaScript together with
  the Apache-2.0 code, which is why package.json says "Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-2.1-or-later".

Bundled songs (CC BY 3.0)
  src/inframe/music_library/ holds songs that are not part of inframe's Apache-2.0 code. Each keeps its own license, CC BY 3.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/), which asks for attribution and a note of changes; the title, author, source, license
  and changes of every song are in src/inframe/music_library/CREDITS.md (also in library.json, with a SHA-256 of each file), which ships in the wheel and is listed
  as a license file. This is why pyproject.toml says "Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-2.1-or-later AND CC-BY-3.0". The wheel metadata and the credits
  are written from the Openverse and Jamendo records of the songs; the licenses were not checked with the artists [unverified].

Python dependencies
  PyAV wheels bundle FFmpeg libraries under the LGPL; they are linked dynamically and not modified. The optional `tracking` extra
  pulls in a package that bundles a GPL-built FFmpeg on macOS; it is not part of the default install. The `music` extra and the dev
  group pull in python-soxr and a libsndfile build (LGPL-2.1). See the Licenses section of README.md.

